From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:19:38 -0600
Subject: test/waitid: accept -ETIME for a fired linked timeout
References: 7.4 build fix
Git-repo: https://github.com/axboe/liburing
Git-commit: 5ff75106b614b3e8f28ad578a45179f295ff56da
Patch-mainline: yes

A linked timeout that fires and cancels a waitid request now completes
with -ETIME, like it does for other requests. Older kernels completed
it with 1. Accept both.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 test/waitid.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/waitid.c b/test/waitid.c
index 54e187fc384f..1bbfbe0dcbb6 100644
--- a/test/waitid.c
+++ b/test/waitid.c
@@ -89,7 +89,9 @@ static int test_noexit(struct io_uring *ring)
 			fprintf(stderr, "cqe wait: %d\n", ret);
 			return T_EXIT_FAIL;
 		}
-		if (cqe->user_data == 2 && cqe->res != 1) {
+		/* older kernels complete a fired linked timeout with 1 */
+		if (cqe->user_data == 2 &&
+		    !(cqe->res == -ETIME || cqe->res == 1)) {
 			fprintf(stderr, "timeout res: %d\n", cqe->res);
 			return T_EXIT_FAIL;
 		}
-- 
